e/13996642/state.json" "file_sha256" "47b94d1f8c373ef374e750558c0cbdc64980888e0614b964231a50eb4e3186de"} {"question" "q-109940" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $-10x+5y\\ge -5?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/state.json" "file_sha256" "47b94d1f8c373ef374e750558c0cbdc64980888e0614b964231a50eb4e3186de"} {"question" "q-109940" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we convert the inequality into slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10x+5y & \\ge -5 \\\\ 5y & \\ge 10x-5 \\\\ y & \\ge 2x-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we proceed as usual. We start by drawing the corresponding straight line $y=2x-1.$ Since the inequality involves a 'greater than *or equal to*' sign, the line $y=2x-1$ itself is part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a solid line.\n\nThen, we need to decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality $y\\ge 2x-1$ refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* or equal to those on the line $y=2x-1,$ so we shade *above* the line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/a9eef4f75cb108bd00fa1230a4be9f5b9edfc21d0ff7f999a3ca8aeb212f08b7.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/state.json" "file_sha256" "47b94d1f8c373ef374e750558c0cbdc64980888e0614b964231a50eb4e3186de"} {"question" "q-109940" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b460bba77719b4f78be355ada84d06e8ca0a4e1640f504f293bd45d88f7dac64"} {"question" "q-109940" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/state.json" "file_sha256" "47b94d1f8c373ef374e750558c0cbdc64980888e0614b964231a50eb4e3186de"} {"question" "q-109940" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/2ae1370dda61376a0c8b684a33f3722620aef05ee289f0a83591546e49221389.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/2f186f14dde18a41004fd77e7280686f32bfc97c9c35f722e5c799c498a36a50.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/419a5f107674817f111a0eed14a49cc91d007d592b61e2c0c5440967f607a356.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/b1fc6cc7406d0f47b142949371b66c59aac6bcdf8bdc7dbc62a113e063642fe2.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/bb3db9d0eaa602c87df225b21be99c0346c72ec142bb498b92671495bc77858a.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/state.json" "file_sha256" "47b94d1f8c373ef374e750558c0cbdc64980888e0614b964231a50eb4e3186de"} {"question" "q-109940" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/419a5f107674817f111a0eed14a49cc91d007d592b61e2c0c5440967f607a356.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/state.json" "file_sha256" "47b94d1f8c373ef374e750558c0cbdc64980888e0614b964231a50eb4e3186de"} {"question" "q-109949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/assets/feed76c05adc7d92f080edf65cc9b94a336d2833397e43c34beb350dc3be514e.png)\n\nFind the inequality that describes the shaded region shown above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/state.json" "file_sha256" "47b94d1f8c373ef374e750558c0cbdc64980888e0614b964231a50eb4e3186de"} {"question" "q-109949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The border-line is a vertical line passing through the point $(3,0).$ Therefore, the line has the equation $x=3.$\n\nNow, we need to decide which inequality symbol to use. Since the line is dashed, we will use a strict inequality. Since the shaded region is to the *left* of the line, the inequality refers to the $x$-values that are *less than* those on the line $x=3.$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\nx<3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/state.json" "file_sha256" "47b94d1f8c373ef374e750558c0cbdc64980888e0614b964231a50eb4e3186de"} {"question" "q-109949" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b460bba77719b4f78be355ada84d06e8ca0a4e1640f504f293bd45d88f7dac64"} {"question" "q-109949" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996642/state.json" "file_sha256" "47b94d1f8c373ef374e750558c0cbdc64980888e0614b964231a50eb4e3186de"} {"question" "q-109949" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x<3"] ["math" "x>3"] ["math" "y<3"] ["math" "y=x+3"] ["math" "y\\le 3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academ